    {
      "title": "Tata Sons rejects Noel Tata's request for Sept 17 board meeting recording",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/tata-sons-rejects-noel-tata-s-request-for-sept-17-board-meeting-recording-126111300995_1.html",
      "description": "Tata Sons has rejected Tata Trusts Chairman Noel Tata's request for sharing an audio-video recording of proceedings of a board meeting held on September 17 in which N Chandrasekaran was reappointed as the chairman of the largest conglomerate's holding company.\nNoel, the only dissenter on the vote for the reappointment, had sought the recordings through a series of communications to Tata Sons since the board meeting, which brought out the differences between the top echelons of the salt-to-software group, with the management of Tata Sons on one side and its biggest shareholder on the other.\n\"Video recording is mandated when one or more Directors attend online.  Company has never in the past had a practice of sharing audio/ video recording of in-person meeting,\" Tata Sons' company secretary Suprakash Mukhopadhyay wrote to Tata Trusts on November 9.\nThe recording is not required to be either retained or shared with anybody, including directors, the letter reads.\nEmails sent to Tata So",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-13T10:52:42"
    }
